            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good. I used 2 large sweet potatoes and boiled them with skin for 50 minutes. I used three medium butternut squashes and boiled them for 30 minutes with skin. Once done I peeled and placed in my food processor - which I highly recommend doing. The squash and potatoes mixed beautifully together(no strings or seeds) I added the rest of the ingredients and poured into my pie crust. I used the marshmallows and my kids ate it up. Again. I suggest using a food processor/blender to mix the squash and potato - makes the process so much easier and the pie ends up looking better too. If you like pecans you can add them to the batter and/or top of the pie with the marshmallows - it's yummy too!"
          },
          {
